            %p where the first map is inverse to composition with the Yoneda embedding, the second map is the equivalence constructed previously, and the third map is composition with the Yoneda embedding.
            %p
              Be careful to note that the first equivalence has not yet been shown to be natural in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
